    <parallel-safe reason="Edits only ComposeAiToolbar.tsx + ComposeEditor.tsx (the BubbleMenu). Disjoint from 110 (BFF) and 112 (ConversationPane/formatter). No file overlap with any Wave-1 sibling.">true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    UAT defect #3a + owner refinement (2026-07-10): the inline selection popup renders with broken layout AND
    mixes formatting controls with AI actions. Owner decision: the inline popup must be **AI functions ONLY** —
    REMOVE the formatting controls from the BubbleMenu (formatting stays in the persistent TOP toolbar), and the
    popup must be openable **two ways**: (a) select text, (b) **right-click at a point** (point insertion) — with
    the browser's native context menu SUPPRESSED inside the Compose editor. Layout root cause to fix along the
    way: `ComposeAiToolbar` returns a Fragment whose first child is a bare `&lt;ToolbarDivider/&gt;` + a second
    `&lt;Toolbar&gt;` mounted as bare children of the BubbleMenu flex row; the divider has no Toolbar context and
    the buttons overflow. Result: a single clean AI-only Toolbar, opened on selection OR right-click.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Frontend engineer fluent in TipTap BubbleMenu + Fluent UI v9 Toolbar/ToolbarButton/ToolbarDivider composition
    and `makeStyles` token-based styling (ADR-021). You correct a Toolbar-composition bug without changing the
    action set, dispatch behavior, or the disabled-until-registered gating.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The inline popup is a single, clean, AI-ONLY Fluent Toolbar (the 5 AI actions + overflow) — NO formatting
    controls (those remain in the persistent top toolbar, untouched), properly-contextualized divider, no
    overflow (wrap or width-cap). It opens on (a) text selection AND (b) right-click at a caret point; inside the
    Compose editor the browser's native context menu is suppressed (contextmenu preventDefault) and the AI
    toolbar opens at the click/caret point instead. Dispatch wiring (handleActionClick → composeActionBridge) and
    the disabled-until-bindingId gating are unchanged; selection-dependent actions still act on the current
    selection if any.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Files: `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx:482-485` (the Fragment `&lt;&gt;&lt;ToolbarDivider/&gt;&lt;Toolbar .../&gt;`),
      `:357-363` (`styles.toolbar` re-imposing display:flex/columnGap over the Fluent Toolbar), `:219-260` (the 5
      DEFAULT_ACTIONS, each shipping `bindingId:''` → disabled until `registerComposeAiToolbarAction`). Host:
      `ComposeEditor.tsx:461-470` (`styles.bubbleMenu`, a center-aligned plain flex row), `:849-885` (the
      formatting `&lt;Toolbar&gt;`), `:848` (BubbleMenu), `:892-899` (where `&lt;ComposeAiToolbar/&gt;` is mounted).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="fix-toolbar-composition" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx</file>
      <file purpose="host-bubblemenu-and-toolbar" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <notes>
      AI-ONLY popup: remove the formatting `&lt;Toolbar&gt;` from the BubbleMenu content; the popup renders ONE
      Fluent `&lt;Toolbar&gt;` containing only the AI actions (+ overflow), with the divider in-context and
      flexWrap/maxWidth so nothing overflows. Drop the redundant `display:flex`/`columnGap` override in
      `styles.toolbar`. Do NOT touch the persistent top formatting toolbar in ComposeEditor — formatting stays
      there. RIGHT-CLICK TRIGGER: TipTap BubbleMenu is selection-driven, so a right-click/point trigger needs an
      explicit handler — wire a ProseMirror `handleDOMEvents.contextmenu` (or an editor-level `onContextMenu`) that
      calls `preventDefault()` inside the editor and opens the AI toolbar at the click/caret position (use a
      controlled/floating popover anchored to the click point, or set a transient selection at the caret to drive
      the BubbleMenu). Both triggers (selection + right-click) coexist. Semantic tokens (ADR-021); verify dark mode.
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project (E2E DoD)">This is a UI-render defect: DoD is a render/DOM assertion (React Testing Library or the project's component test harness) that the popup mounts as a single Toolbar with the divider inside Toolbar context and no overflow — not merely a build-pass. The toolbar must also be shown MOUNTED + REACHABLE in the BubbleMenu.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; no hard-coded colors; dark-mode correct.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT change the 5 action ids, dispatch wiring, or the disabled-until-bindingId gating (that is task 048's contract).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No auth/fetch changes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

