  <justification component="No new component — corrects existing Toolbar composition">
    <existing>ComposeAiToolbar + the BubbleMenu Toolbar already exist (task 030).</existing>
    <extension>Refactor the existing composition (fold AI items into the host Toolbar / fix divider context + overflow). No new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The inline AI affordance — the primary FR-14 surface — renders visibly broken, undermining the whole inline-AI UX the owner just tested.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load the triage note + task 030 + ADR-021. Read `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx:357-363/482-485` and `ComposeEditor.tsx:461-470/848-899` to confirm the composition + the persistent top formatting toolbar.</step>
    <step order="1">Make the BubbleMenu popup AI-ONLY: remove the formatting `&lt;Toolbar&gt;` from the popup content; render one Fluent `&lt;Toolbar&gt;` with only the AI actions (+ overflow), divider in-context, flexWrap/maxWidth so nothing overflows; remove the orphaned top-level divider; drop the redundant `display:flex`/`columnGap` in `styles.toolbar`. Do NOT touch the top formatting toolbar.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the right-click/point-insertion trigger: wire a ProseMirror `handleDOMEvents.contextmenu` (or editor-level `onContextMenu`) that `preventDefault()`s the browser menu inside the editor and opens the AI toolbar at the click/caret point (works with NO selection). Keep the existing text-selection trigger working too.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify dark mode + semantic tokens. Add/extend a component test asserting: (a) popup contains ONLY AI actions (no formatting buttons); (b) one Toolbar, divider in-context, no overflow; (c) contextmenu handler calls preventDefault + opens the AI toolbar; (d) right-click with no selection still opens it; (e) the top formatting toolbar is untouched/formatting still reachable.</step>
    <step order="4">Recompile the Spaarke.Compose.Components package per code-page-deploy cache rules; run the component tests + lint.</step>
    <step order="5">code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Report for the main session to update TASK-INDEX + commit.</step>
  </steps>

